WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.279
Sharkboy and Lavagirl are back for an Avengers-style
sequel, but when they're captured by alien

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:11.019
invaders, a group of super-powered kids including
their daughter Guppy have to come together

00:00:11.019 --> 00:00:12.559
to try and rescue them.

00:00:12.559 --> 00:00:16.850
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video we're diving into the ending of

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.640
We Can Be Heroes to reveal all the secret
clues you missed that set up the movie's big

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:22.640
twist.

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:25.429
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:30.300
We Can Be Heroes initially tricks us into
thinking we're watching a pretty typical alien

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:35.120
invasion movie where superheroes will save
the day, however, at the end of the film,

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.510
we learn this has all be a giant ruse!

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:42.719
The aliens aren't here to openly attack us
but to secretly support us by training the

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:46.440
next generation of superheroes in the awesome
power of teamwork

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:51.010
so the super-kids can take over from their
parents and fix the earth's many problems

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:52.399
as soon as possible.

00:00:52.399 --> 00:00:57.250
For their plan to work, the aliens infiltrated
both the government and Heroics HQ.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:02.890
But it wasn't just the President's name, Neil
Anami, which is 'I'm an Alien' spelled backwards,

00:01:02.890 --> 00:01:05.180
that pointed to the movie's twist ending.

00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:10.850
A big clue to the surprise twist was also
hidden in the name of the aliens' home planet,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.560
which was called Ogima.

00:01:12.560 --> 00:01:17.070
If you spell Ogima backwards, it turns out
to be "Amigo", which is the Spanish word for

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:18.070
friend!

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:21.360
"A message from the supreme commander of the
aliens.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:23.140
We are from the planet Ogima."

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.470
So, the fact the aliens were really here to
help us humans rather than harm us was predicted

00:01:28.470 --> 00:01:30.740
right from the beginning of the movie!

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:35.420
Interestingly, writer-director Robert Rodriguez
also indulged in a bit of backwards naming

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:40.689
in the original Sharkboy and Lavagirl movie,
calling an unfinished robot character Tobor,

00:01:40.689 --> 00:01:43.270
which is robot spelled in reverse.

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:46.360
Even before we find out the name of the alien
planet though,

00:01:46.360 --> 00:01:50.750
there's another huge hint to the film's finale
when Missy sees Miracle Guy being wheeled

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:55.479
into an ambulance after the movie's opening
alien attack and, in an effort to reassure

00:01:55.479 --> 00:02:00.470
her and stop her worrying, her dad tells her:
"That is just a training exercise, probably.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.009
A… a 'what if'."

00:02:03.009 --> 00:02:07.280
In fact, it turns out that everything Missy
and her super-powered pals go through after

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:10.830
this in the movie
is indeed a big training exercise organised

00:02:10.830 --> 00:02:15.580
by the aliens to ready the kids to step into
their parents' super-shoes and save the world!

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:20.580
There are also several tell-tale signs as
soon as we meet Ojo that there's much more

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.090
to her than meets the eye.

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:26.150
First of all, she's not dressed like any of
the other kids, who are all wearing T-shirts,

00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:31.820
jeans, and other casual clothes, in contrast
to her smarter white blouse and black trousers.

00:02:31.820 --> 00:02:37.140
And that seems appropriate because, after
all, she is the aliens' Supreme Commander!

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:42.170
On top of that, her name, Ojo, is the Spanish
word for 'eye' and can also mean 'insight',

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:46.690
all of which fits her character perfectly
as she's all about vision and foreshadowing

00:02:46.690 --> 00:02:50.590
what's going to happen, drawing things on
her tablet which later come true.

00:02:50.590 --> 00:02:55.710
But that's not all; the word 'ojo' can also
be used in Spanish to warn someone to 'watch

00:02:55.710 --> 00:03:00.190
out!' or 'look out!', which is also fitting
as Ojo isn't what she appears to be;

00:03:00.190 --> 00:03:03.000
she's not a human girl, she's actually an
alien!

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.980
I love these little clues and extra layers
of meaning that Mexican-American Robert Rodriguez

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.770
gives the film by including Spanish words
like this

00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:15.840
and the fact he continues to cast diversely
including lots of Latinx actors, as he's done

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.070
on many of his previous projects.

00:03:18.070 --> 00:03:22.450
By the way, if you were watching like a hawk
during the scene in the tunnels,

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.700
you might have just caught the picture Ojo
drew of herself with her alien tentacles on

00:03:26.700 --> 00:03:32.010
display which flashed by in a millisecond
as Missy was swiping past on Ojo's tablet.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:36.761
And there was another sneaky clue that it
was Ojo who was really in charge of the aliens

00:03:36.761 --> 00:03:41.510
all along when the kids discovered the president
on the alien mother-ship and overheard him

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:42.800
discussing the takeover.

00:03:42.800 --> 00:03:45.510
"How long before the takeover begins?"

00:03:45.510 --> 00:03:49.040
"According to the supreme commander, less
than an hour."

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.310
"Ever wonder why we bother with all this when
she already knows how it's gonna turn out?"

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:57.870
That's a reference to Ojo's ability to see
the future and a clue that she's the one really

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.180
giving the orders.

00:03:59.180 --> 00:04:04.830
Did you also notice Ms Granada's rather odd,
exaggerated manner from the start which was

00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:08.110
perhaps a clue to her alien nature?

00:04:08.110 --> 00:04:12.640
For example, when she enters the Control Room
at HQ, she walks more like a model sashaying

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:14.010
down a catwalk.

00:04:14.010 --> 00:04:18.430
And then, there's the slightly strange way
she often holds her hands out to the sides,

00:04:18.430 --> 00:04:23.410
almost as if she's either performing a dance
in a musical or trying to keep her balance!

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:27.560
Maybe that's because of the mass of alien
tentacles she's having to hide in her human

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:28.560
disguise.

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:33.490
That the new Heroics kids can succeed where
the adults failed is also cleverly emphasised

00:04:33.490 --> 00:04:34.590
throughout the movie.

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:39.070
For example, the many butterflies dotted around
Missy's room right at the beginning of the

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:43.290
film, symbolise the fact that she and the
other kids represent a new beginning, a fresh

00:04:43.290 --> 00:04:45.340
chance to get things right.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:49.380
While the rainbow on Guppy's necklace sends
a subtle message from the start that these

00:04:49.380 --> 00:04:55.030
super-kids are humanity's hope for a better
world, as Ojo confirms at the end of the movie.

00:04:55.030 --> 00:05:00.120
This new generation of heroes is all about
teamwork, rather than squabbling among themselves

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:01.310
like their parents.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:06.130
And to accentuate just how different they
are to the previous generation, the new Heroics

00:05:06.130 --> 00:05:08.440
also have an entirely different look.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:13.960
Gone are the colourful costumes and hard-to-see-out-of
masks often favoured by superheroes including

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.960
many of their mums and dads, such as Sharkboy
and Lavagirl.

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.700
"All superheroes have costumes.

00:05:18.700 --> 00:05:22.060
Pads, fake muscles, tons of useless buckles."

00:05:22.060 --> 00:05:23.620
"Underwear on the outside."

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:25.970
"Masks you can barely see out of."

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.430
"That's why they were able to pick out our
parents so easily."

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.730
"We have to blend in."

00:05:29.730 --> 00:05:35.150
Instead, those highly visible costumes are
replaced by more practical uniforms in muted

00:05:35.150 --> 00:05:36.150
colours.

00:05:36.150 --> 00:05:38.240
"So what are we supposed to be looking at?"

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:39.240
"The future."

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:43.460
